# K03-EXPLICIT-RECEIVER-FRAMES (the author, 2026-10-06): merge's Frames at the unit's root -- short, compact, the
# completed vertical spelling with two operands, the Frame as the sole content of an anonymous Structure,
# `u: (merge: Model)`, and a parenthesized operand, `merge: (Model)` -- read by methods as their hidden inputs:
# 1 + 3 + 3 + 2 = 9.  The vertical and compact spellings translate as the short ones do, byte for byte.  Entry 7.
Model:
    size_t: x 1U
end: Model
Extra:
    size_t: z 2U
end: Extra
r: merge: Model
s: merge(Model Extra)
t:
. merge:
. . Model
. . Extra
---
u: (merge: Model)
w: merge: (Model)
fn: readr () size_t
    return: r\x
end: readr
fn: reads () size_t
    return: s\x + s\z
end: reads
fn: readt () size_t
    return: t\x + t\z
end: readt
fn: readu () size_t
    return: u\x + w\x
end: readu
size_t: got 0U
got: readr() + reads() + readt() + readu()
if: got != 9U
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 81; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
